<h1>BPP</h1>
<p>
(definition)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
The class of <a href="language.html"><em>languages</em></a> for which a membership computation by a <a href="probablturng.html"><em>probabilistic Turing machine</em></a> halts in <a href="polynomialtm.html"><em>polynomial time</em></a> with the right answer (accept or reject) at least 2/3 of the time. "BPP" means "<strong>B</strong>ounded error <strong>P</strong>robability in <strong>P</strong>olynomial" time.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Also known as</strong> bounded error probability in polynomial time.
</p>

<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="zpp.html"><em>ZPP</em></a>, <a href="rp.html"><em>RP</em></a>, <a href="np.html"><em>NP</em></a>, <a href="complexityClass.html"><em>complexity class</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
By repeating the run, the chance of error may be arbitrarily reduced. </p> 
<p> After <a href="../terms.html#Hirv01">[Hirv01, page 19]</a>.</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>
